</div>
<p>A 2-layer GNN on a batch of 1,000 nodes — 5% of this graph — already touches 90% of it. At three layers it’s the entire graph. The batch size stopped controlling the working set some time ago.</p>
<p>The practical read: for deep GNNs the interesting question usually isn’t the model, it’s what you’re willing to <em>not</em> look at — sampling, historical embeddings, or partitioning the graph and eating the cut edges. Full-batch propagation <span class="citation" data-cites="kipf2017semi">(Kipf and Welling 2017)</span> is fine right up until the receptive field stops fitting, and then it isn’t.</p>
</section>
